# The packages the Python tooling uses directly, each at an exact version. `make lock` turns this into requirements.txt:
# the same packages PLUS everything they pull in, every one with the sha256 of its files, which is what gets installed.
#
# Output of build.py depends on these: Markdown renders the section texts that feed content_version, Pillow encodes the
# images. A different version can make a deploy "update" things nobody edited.
# Bump rule: change the pin here, `make lock venv`, `make deps test`, review `make plan` for unexpected updates, update
# AGENTS.md + CHANGELOG.md.
